From 7afc40c0c233f3ec358a6deabf95fed717bf5816 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:48:30 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Optional CUDA path for light competition and seed
 dispersal

qmake CONFIG+=cuda builds ilandc with src/gpu/iland_gpu.cu (CUDA runtime
linked statically). At runtime the GPU is used if a device is present,
unless ILAND_GPU=0; on any CUDA error the model continues on the CPU.

- Light (Model::applyPattern/readPattern, non-torus): the GPU initialises
  the LIF grid, builds the height grid, applies all patterns (atomic
  multiply) and computes each tree's raw light sum; the species-specific
  LRI correction and resource-unit sums stay on the CPU (Tree::readLIF is
  split into lightSum() and setLightResourceIndex()). The GPU completes the
  height grid before applying patterns; the CPU code interleaves both per
  resource unit. ILAND_GPU_VALIDATE=1 compares each year with the CPU:
  light grid within 4e-7, raw LRI within 5e-7 relative, height grid
  identical; the CPU's own interleaving changes LRI by up to 128%.
- Seed dispersal (non-torus): kernel convolution, long distance dispersal
  (Philox random numbers seeded from iLand's generator) and scaling on the
  GPU; statistically equivalent to the CPU, not bit-identical.
- Model keeps the GPU members in every build so plugins compiled without
  ILAND_CUDA see the same class layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F4XU94RLz4kFVSs5LcJjTK
